      "dcDescription": [
        "\"361-12 \"Woman's woven sash or belt (sis or esdzán bizís); cotton, wool, dye; l. 250 cm. (without fringe), w. 8.8 cm.; ca. 1870-1880.\\nSash of commercial cotton string in warp float weave. The red, orange, and green warps are two-ply Z-S spin split from a four-ply wool yarn and re-spun. These belts for securing the woman's dress were originally woven of blue yarn, but later other colors came to be preferred, with red as a favorite (Franciscan Fathers 1910:248-249). The edge stripes on this specimen are uneven and that combined with a very lovely pattern gives an unusual effect. The loom is ess"
